From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] egui-winit (AROS): pictures from the clipboard for Cmd/Ctrl+V

Crate: egui-winit 0.37.0 (storytold/egui 6d518fc7) with 0001-0003.
Date: 2026-11-07
Problem: with a picture and no text on the clipboard, Cmd/Ctrl+V sends
  Event::PasteImage from Clipboard::get_image() on the desktops; on AROS that
  function had no source, so Ctrl+V did nothing (WordCraft 0.16.0 and
  GridCraft 0.17.0 paste pictures from that event; their menus' Paste worked
  through the host).
  Also get() answered a clipboard without text with the in-process copy,
  Some("") when there was none, so the image fallback was never reached.
Rationale: aros-gui-sys 0004 reads the clipboard's picture through
  datatypes; get_image() converts its RGBA to a ColorImage. An unreadable
  picture is logged and nothing is pasted, as for other platforms' errors.
  get() returns the system clipboard's text on AROS and the in-process copy
  only when it holds something.
Prerequisites: aros-gui-sys 0004-clipboard-pictures.patch.
Upstream-status: candidate for the AROS contrib crate store (not submitted).
Verification: see the egui-aros build records.
Removal: with 0001.
---
diff -ruN egui-winit-0.37.0.orig/src/clipboard.rs egui-winit-0.37.0/src/clipboard.rs
--- egui-winit-0.37.0.orig/src/clipboard.rs	2026-11-07 13:15:32
+++ egui-winit-0.37.0/src/clipboard.rs	2026-11-07 13:30:37
@@ -244,10 +244,11 @@
         expect(clippy::needless_pass_by_ref_mut, clippy::unnecessary_wraps)
     )]
     pub fn get(&mut self) -> Option<String> {
+        // AROS: the system clipboard's text. The in-process copy only stands in when it holds
+        // something (a copy the system clipboard could not take); an empty one would turn
+        // Cmd/Ctrl+V on a picture into an empty text paste instead of Event::PasteImage.
         #[cfg(target_os = "aros")]
-        if let Some(text) = aros::get() {
-            return Some(text);
-        }
+        return aros::get().or_else(|| (!self.clipboard.is_empty()).then(|| self.clipboard.clone()));
 
         #[cfg(all(
             any(
@@ -398,6 +399,21 @@
         expect(clippy::needless_pass_by_ref_mut, clippy::unused_self)
     )]
     pub fn get_image(&mut self) -> Option<egui::ColorImage> {
+        // AROS: a picture another program put on clipboard unit 0, read through datatypes
+        // (aros-gui-sys). Cmd/Ctrl+V with no text on the clipboard then sends Event::PasteImage
+        // as on the other desktops.
+        #[cfg(target_os = "aros")]
+        return match aros_gui_sys::clipboard::read_picture() {
+            aros_gui_sys::clipboard::ClipboardImage::Pixels { width, height, rgba } => {
+                Some(egui::ColorImage::from_rgba_unmultiplied([width as usize, height as usize], &rgba))
+            }
+            aros_gui_sys::clipboard::ClipboardImage::Unreadable(why) => {
+                log::warn!("AROS clipboard picture: {why}");
+                None
+            }
+            aros_gui_sys::clipboard::ClipboardImage::None => None,
+        };
+
         #[cfg(all(
             any(
                 target_os = "linux",
